	<Property Name="NI.Lib.Description" Type="Str">A document defines a link to an external file. This document is uniquely identified by its Identifier. The document also has an optional Name attribute which is meant to contain a human-friendly identifier, and a FileName attribute. The FileName is used to identify the type of document and should contain an extension so that the appropriate application is launched when the user requests to view the document content. An optional Description can also be specified.
        
Documents are unique among siblings by their Identifier property.  This makes it possible for two different entities (ex: two different product units) to refer to the same document.</Property>
